<title>USA: Digital Video prices units at $1,000.</title>
<headline>Digital Video prices units at $1,000.</headline>
<dateline>SANTA CLARA, Calif. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Digital Video Systems Inc said its registration statement for a secondary public offering of $26,450,000 of units consisting of common stock and warrants was declared effective.</p>
<p>The units are being offered at an initial price of $1,000 each. D.H. Blair is the underwriter of the offering.  </p>
<p>The company said the offering was declared effective and priced on November 21.</p>
</text>
